Subject: vfs, server: idle base directories close their descriptors, so a volume no client uses holds only its root's (slates A-838 2f5b207d2)
Why: kiln's restarted Slates daemon on adacachy held 79,038 base directory descriptors two minutes after its start: every listed directory kept its descriptor for the volume's life. Fixed on Slates main (A-838, 2f5b207d2) with its tests; the idle sweep closes a directory unused a whole interval and reacquires it by path at its next use. This carries it until the next re-vendor, which drops this change as upstream's own.

